  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **cold & wet**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 9 archived performances [5]\n- **i got a weasel**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [5]\n- **stacey**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 7 archived performances [5]\n- **gladiola heartbreaker**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 8 archived performances [5]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: tick, seconds, never squeal, up on the hill, common bitch, el camino, old queen cole, papa zit, squelch the weasel, wayne's pet youngin', fat lenny, lmlyp [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween1989-00-00.fm.sbd.flac16** (recommended): soundboard; 16 songs; 41 min; rated 4.33/5 by 3 [1]. Said about its sound: FM reception fades briefly at the start, and the tape has noticeable hiss [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The Fiendz also performed at this WTSR Radiothon event [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween1989-00-00.fm.sbd.flac16**: taped by Josh Keats; transferred by Josh Keats; source: SBD > FM broadcast [1]. Also: Archive systems misdate the file due to missing month and day in the filename; Encoded directly from a master cassette stored for nearly fifteen years without noise reduction [1][3]",
